<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>1.12.1: Using the Slope Formula</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00261</md:content-id>
    <md:title>1.12.1: Using the Slope Formula</md:title>
    <md:uuid>5417c5d2-b25e-4488-9b99-ba9cb7ab98e4</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section id="sect-00001"><title>Warm Up Activity</title>
<para id="para-00001">Use the slope formula, \( m =\frac{y_2-y_1}{x_2-x_1}\), to find the slope of the line through the given points.</para>
<exercise id="exer-00001">
  <problem id="prob-00001">
    <para id="para-00002">\( (1, -2) \) and \( (3, 4) \)</para>
    </problem><solution id="sol-00001">
    
    
  
  <para id="para-00003">Compare your answer:</para>
    
    <para id="para-00004">\( m= 3 \)</para>
    
    <para id="para-00005">First, name \( (1, −2) \) as point 1 and \( (3, 4) \) as point 2.</para>
    
    <para id="para-00006">\( (x_1, y_1) \) and \( (x_2, y_2) \)</para>
    
    <para id="para-00007">\( (1,−2) \) and \( (3, 4) \)</para>
    
    <para id="para-00008">Use the slope formula.</para>
    
    <para id="para-00009">\( m=\frac{y_2-y_1}{x_2-x_1} \) 
    </para>
    
    <para id="para-00010">Substitute the values: \( y_2 = 4, y_1 = -2, x_2 = 3, x_1 = 1 \).</para>
    
    <para id="para-00011">\( m=\frac{4-(-2)}{3-(1)} \)</para>
    
    <para id="para-00012">Simplify.</para>
    
    <para id="para-00013">\( m=\frac{6}{2} \)</para>
    
    <para id="para-00014">\( m=3 \)</para>
  
  </solution></exercise>

<exercise id="exer-00002">
  <problem id="prob-00002">
    <para id="para-00015">\( (-2, -3) \) and \( (-7, 4) \)</para>
    </problem><solution id="sol-00002">
    
    
  
  <para id="para-00016">Compare your answer:</para>
    
    <para id="para-00017">\( m=-\frac{7}{5} \)</para>
    
    <para id="para-00018">First, name \( (−2, −3) \) as point 1 and \( (−7, 4) \) as point 2.</para>
    
    <para id="para-00019">\( (x_1, y_1) \) and \( (x_2, y_2) \)</para>
    
    <para id="para-00020">\( (−2,−3)\) and \( (−7, 4) \)</para>
    
    <para id="para-00021">Use the slope formula.</para>
    
    <para id="para-00022">\( m=\frac{y_2-y_1}{x_2-x_1} \)</para>
    
    <para id="para-00023">Substitute the values: \( y_2 = 4, y_1 = −3, x_2 = −7, x_1 = −2 \).</para>
    
    <para id="para-00024">\( m= \frac{4-(-3)}{-7-(-2)} \)</para>
    
    <para id="para-00025">Simplify.</para>
    
    <para id="para-00026">\( m= \frac{7}{-5} \)</para>
    
    <para id="para-00027">\( m= -\frac{7}{5} \)</para>
  
  </solution></exercise>

</section>
</content>
